#!/usr/bin/env bash

set -Eeuo pipefail
umask 077

# ============================================================
# Proxmox VE configuration recovery tool
# ============================================================
#
# Changelog
# 1.14 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 SSH R6, 2026-10-08)
#   - Bind parser-only and PREVIOUS-main temporary objects to their original
#     device/inode and full owned descriptors; reject foreign replacement.
#   - Recheck ssh.service active at final commit and late rollback gates;
#     momentary service health is not proof of HUP completion.
#   - Correct SSH helper filename and maintain unchanged VERSION=1.14.
#   - Dateifreigabe, Backup 1.6 and all non-SSH domains stay unchanged.
#
# 1.14 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 SSH R5, 2026-10-08)
#   - Reverify LIVE PREVIOUS/TARGET and external Include after private cleanup
#     and result-write I/O in SAME_STATE, REFUSED, and ROLLED_BACK branches.
#   - A detected FOREIGN/AMBIGUOUS final state is CRITICAL; never blind rollback.
#   - Correct RC20 wrapper claim; product version remains 1.14 (SSH R5).
#   - Dateifreigabe, Backup 1.6 and all non-SSH domains are unchanged.
#

# 1.14 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 SSH R4, 2026-10-08)
#   - Recheck TARGET at late commit/after cleanup and before reporting success;
#     detected foreign changes are CRITICAL, not falsely COMMITTED.
#   - Check immutable private directory mtime at cleanup admission; allow
#     explicit stage-root and own cleanup mtime transitions only.
#   - SSH R4 remains DRAFT; no SSH host mutation or promotion performed.
#
# 1.14 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 SSH R3, 2026-10-08)
#   - Cleanup now rejects missing as well as foreign entries in owned private
#     trees; stage remainder derives solely from proven source-renames.
#   - Escrow and quarantine cleanup require the full ownership inventory;
#     incomplete/ambiguous cleanup is CRITICAL, never silent COMMITTED.
#   - SSH R3 remains DRAFT; hostvalidation H0-H9 and promotion pending.
#
# 1.14 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 SSH R2, 2026-10-08)
#   - Repair in-process signals immediately after Main/Drop-in renames: recover
#     transaction state from owned filesystem descriptors, not post-syscall flags.
#   - Enforce secure SSH root/parent admission and atomic no-replace directory
#     renames; preserve foreign stage/escrow objects instead of blind cleanup.
#   - Define an irreversible COMMIT cleanup boundary; post-commit failures are
#     CRITICAL and never misrepresented as rollbackable. Product remains 1.14.
#   - R2 remains DRAFT; no Proxmox SSH host mutation or promotion performed.
#
# 1.14 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 SSH R1, 2026-10-08)
#   - C-29 SSH introduces a domain-local two-object transaction for sshd_config
#     and sshd_config.d, with strict staged parser admission and exact ownership.
#   - FOREIGN/AMBIGUOUS states fail closed; rollback is conditional, not blind.
#     Same-state performs neither rewrites nor reload; Dateifreigabe stays out of scope.
#   - HUP is logged as a reload request, never a proven daemon reload completion.
#   - SSH R1 is a DRAFT only: independent Proxmox host validation H0-H9 pending.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# 1.13 (C-29 PASSWORDS R2 FIX, 2026-10-08)
#   - A failed stat() on a newly created PASSWORDS temporary auth file now
#     latches unproven cleanup before returning. The transaction must report
#     the critical cleanup state (RC 78) instead of an ordinary failed write.
#   - No blind deletion without proven temporary-file ownership; other C-29
#     domains are unchanged. SCRIPT_VERSION remains 1.13.
# 1.13 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 PASSWORDS R1, 2026-10-07)
#   - C-29 PASSWORDS adds a domain-local transactional restore for user.cfg and
#     priv/shadow.cfg. Product development advances from validated 1.12 to 1.13
#     and PASSWORDS starts at R1; Storage/VM/C-28 behavior is otherwise retained.
#   - The complete authentication writer lock set is held in native Proxmox order
#     (domains -> TFA -> user -> token -> shadow) across PREVIOUS capture, QUIESCE,
#     TARGET apply, validation, commit or rollback. The helper pins the current
#     /etc/pve FUSE mount and refuses cluster/corosync scope for this standalone R1.
#   - Reader-visible mixed auth state is fail-closed with a minimal empty user.cfg
#     QUIESCE before password transition. TARGET shadow is made live before TARGET
#     user.cfg; rollback keeps QUIESCE until PREVIOUS shadow is exact, then restores
#     PREVIOUS user.cfg. FOREIGN/AMBIGUOUS pairs are never blindly overwritten.
#   - Strict raw schema/duplicate checks are combined with the installed native
#     Proxmox parsers. R1 refuses API-token metadata/secrets, token ACL principals,
#     legacy user keys, modern TFA state, custom realms and orphan shadow entries;
#     a PVE user without a password remains valid. No token/TFA/domain merge occurs.
#   - Same-state TARGET/PREVIOUS commits without rewriting auth files. SIGKILL,
#     reboot, kernel panic and power loss remain C-30 scope; existing tickets are
#     not claimed to be revoked by a password restore.
# 1.12 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 VM R3, 2026-10-07)
#   - Standalone-scope admission is hardened fail-closed for dangling Corosync
#     symlinks: Bash checks both existence and symlink objects, and the pinned
#     pmxcfs Perl context applies the same rule before/after live mutation.
#   - VM native-lock admission now reports a neutral verification failure at the
#     caller instead of incorrectly describing every failure as a 10-second
#     timeout. Detailed causes remain emitted by the lock helper itself.
#   - R2 transaction/locking architecture is otherwise unchanged; Storage, C-28,
#     C-30 and other C-29 domains are untouched. SCRIPT_VERSION remains 1.12.
# 1.12 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 VM R2, 2026-10-07)
#   - Corrective VM revision: native QEMU lock path is resolved from the
#     installed PVE::QemuConfig implementation instead of hardcoding one path.
#     While the Bash lock is held, a separate PVE::QemuConfig->lock_config_full()
#     probe must be unable to enter its callback; otherwise VM restore refuses
#     before PREVIOUS capture/live mutation. This makes lock-contract drift
#     fail closed. /var/lock and /run/lock aliases are canonicalized before FD
#     identity checks, so Debian's /var/lock -> /run/lock symlink is handled.
#   - C-29 VM product scope is explicitly standalone-only for 1.12; presence of
#     local or pmxcfs corosync configuration refuses this VM restore path, and
#     the pinned pmxcfs context rechecks that scope before/after live mutation.
#     No generic cluster/cross-type serialization guarantee is claimed.
#   - VM operation admission now declares readlink explicitly, and QEMU-process
#     probing distinguishes pgrep RC1 (no match) from RC>1 (probe failure),
#     refusing fail-closed on process-detection errors.
#   - R1 transaction architecture is otherwise retained; Storage/C-28/C-30 and
#     other C-29 domains are intentionally unchanged. SCRIPT_VERSION remains 1.12.
# 1.12 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 VM R1, 2026-10-07)
#   - First domain-local VM revision after the completed C-29 Storage domain
#     was promoted into the validated 1.11 product baseline.
#   - C-29 VM-domain integration: VM restore now uses the shared transaction
#     state machine with immutable TARGET, stable PREVIOUS, exact ownership
#     gates, exact TARGET-before-commit and PREVIOUS-after-rollback checks.
#   - The native Proxmox per-VM flock remains held across PREVIOUS capture,
#     live mutation, validation, commit or rollback. Live VM-file transitions
#     additionally pin the current /etc/pve FUSE mount so pmxcfs loss cannot
#     redirect a write into an underlying local /etc/pve directory.
#   - Staged VM TARGETs are strict-parsed before mutation with
#     PVE::QemuServer::parse_vm_config(..., 1). Post-write/rollback validation
#     is non-interactive and fails closed on qm diagnostics. Unexpected in-
#     process exits use the same ownership-aware rollback hook as Storage.
#   - Product target version is 1.12. C-29 domain revisions are local to their
#     domain, so VM development starts again at R1. No C-30 behavior is added.
# 1.11 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 R7, 2026-10-06)
#   - A critical session end latches recovery-required for this process. Further
#     restore menu actions and session admission are blocked; backup inspection
#     and exit remain available. Transaction reset does not clear this latch.
#   - Keep the backup timer stopped and retain remaining workdir evidence even
#     if moving it to the emergency directory failed. No in-process override.
#   - Shared post-critical lifecycle policy changes for all restore domains;
#     domain restore bodies and C-28 network logic remain unchanged. Validator
#     deadlines still require host evidence. SCRIPT_VERSION remains 1.11; no C-30.
# 1.11 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 R6, 2026-10-06)
#   - Identical admitted Storage PREVIOUS/TARGET descriptors use a locked no-op
#     instead of rewriting storage.cfg. TARGET validation and the final locked
#     commit gate remain mandatory. This avoids same-byte writes being hidden
#     by PREVIOUS reclassification after a late callback failure.
#     SCRIPT_VERSION remains 1.11. No C-28 or C-30 behavior is changed.
# 1.11 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 R5, 2026-10-06)
#   - Storage temporary-file cleanup is a required postcondition, including
#     in-process exceptions after temporary-file creation. Cleanup only removes
#     an object matching the identity of this operation's own temporary file.
#   - Unproven cleanup remains AMBIGUOUS/CRITICAL through apply, rollback and
#     EXIT handling; exact storage.cfg bytes cannot hide an unresolved artifact.
#     SCRIPT_VERSION remains 1.11. No C-28 or C-30 behavior is changed.
# 1.11 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, C-29 R4, 2026-10-06)
#   - R4 closes the Storage-pilot apply and rollback compare/write races by
#     executing the critical storage.cfg compare/write transition inside
#     PVE::Storage::lock_storage_config(), the same Proxmox cfs lock protocol
#     used by normal storage configuration writers.
#   - Storage live-state gates now verify pmxcfs IPC plus the current /etc/pve
#     FUSE mount and pin that mount through an open directory descriptor during
#     locked writes, preventing fallback writes into an unmounted local path.
#   - `pvesm status` remains outside the cfs lock. Its R4 contract is deliberately
#     limited to command acceptance (RC 0 and no stderr diagnostics); it does not
#     claim that every configured backend is reachable/active. Final TARGET and
#     PREVIOUS identity gates are reacquired under the Proxmox storage lock.
#   - Lock/callback failures are classified by locked postconditions before the
#     transaction decides whether a live mutation occurred; a late cfs-lock
#     callback failure therefore cannot be mislabeled as "no mutation".
#   - R3 TARGET/PREVIOUS prevalidation, explicit transaction states, no-write
#     PREVIOUS rollback, phase-neutral runtime naming and C-28 isolation remain.
#     SCRIPT_VERSION remains 1.11; R4 is a corrective revision, not 1.12.
# 1.10 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, 2026-10-03)
#   - C-28 R6: the offline health fixture no longer assumes that a host has an
#     interface named eth0. Host-validation H1 on localserver001 exposed that
#     portability bug because the real physical port is LAN1. The product
#     connectivity/runtime logic is unchanged from R5.
#   - C-28 R5: package/runtime naming cleanup completes the phase-neutral naming
#     rule for current technical artifacts. The offline harness uses a generic
#     temporary path, and stale R1/R2 revision labels in current comments were
#     neutralized. Connectivity/runtime behavior is unchanged from R4.
#   - C-28 R4: phase-number coupling was removed from runtime identifiers.
#     Connectivity globals, local variables, WORKDIR artifact names and Python
#     heredoc markers now use generic network/connectivity/health names. Stale
#     runtime messages that named the R2 revision were neutralized to the
#     connectivity-watchdog scope. Runtime logic is otherwise unchanged from R3.
#   - C-28 R3: RC0 plus error/Traceback diagnostics now follows the same
#     automatic PREVIOUS rollback/re-apply/health-confirm path as a non-zero
#     TARGET ifreload. The final successful health pass rechecks restored files,
#     ifupdown2 runtime state and the monotonic deadline before commit.
#     PREVIOUS is always re-applied during recovery even when its C-28 health
#     profile is unavailable; lack of a profile still prevents a false success
#     claim and enters the critical/manual-recovery path.
#   - C-28 R2: a live network apply is provisional until a locally derived
#     management profile passes carrier/interface/address/route/MTU and bound
#     gateway probes three consecutive times inside a 10-second deadline.
#     PREVIOUS is captured from the known runtime before live writes and is
#     health-confirmed after automatic rollback. Unsupported/ambiguous topology
#     blocks only live apply and keeps the controlled-reboot restore path. C-28
#     uses no external service, daemon or persistent crash journal.
#   - C-28 connectivity helper functions use the generic network_connectivity_*
#     namespace instead of embedding the project phase number in function names.
#   - Version bump to 1.10.
# 1.9 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, 2026-10-01)
#   - Post-C-26 review: restore_ssh now checks every live SSH write and every
#     rollback write explicitly. A partial cp/rm failure enters a controlled
#     rollback path instead of letting global `set -e` terminate the tool while
#     the restore session is active.
#   - SSH rollback failure is reported as CRITICAL and keeps the automatic
#     backup timer stopped for manual recovery.
#   - Version bump to 1.9.
#   - C-27 R7: before bridge MTUs are neutralized, a first private syntax pass
#     keeps those MTUs intact (while retaining the C-26 fd rewrite). Only the
#     exact reviewed bridge-MTU false-positive may be ignored there, so dependent
#     checks such as VLAN MTU > bridge-parent MTU keep their source information.
#     Pass A records exactly which pre-approved bridges actually emitted that
#     false-positive; pass B neutralizes MTU only for that seen subset, not for
#     every raw allowlisted bridge. Hard validator reasons in both syntax passes
#     (busy, lock-unavailable, isolation) are preserved before generic diagnostic
#     classification, and observed ifupdown2 concurrency is retained across both
#     syntax passes. The real/restored candidate stays unchanged. Ambiguous,
#     duplicate or invalid MTU input fails closed. The workaround is pinned to
#     the exact reviewed ifupdown2 package version plus the C-27-relevant
#     code/configuration files. C-27 does not introduce another SCRIPT_VERSION
#     bump; it extends 1.9.
# 1.8 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, 2026-09-30)
#   - C-26 REVIEW3: Network restore validation handles the ifupdown2 3.3.0
#     `bridge-fd 0` syntax-check regression without changing backed-up values.
#     A frozen candidate tree is captured before validation, and every parser or
#     syntax check uses that same candidate through a private copy. Only
#     unambiguous bridge-fd 0 + STP off/no/default-off stanzas are changed to fd 2
#     inside the throw-away copy. /etc/network itself must be a real directory,
#     copied validation paths are canonicalized before rewriting, and the
#     validation namespace gets a private /var/log so synthetic fd-2 copies are
#     not added to the host's persistent ifupdown2 debug history.
#   - Network validation no longer offers generic KEEP for ifupdown2 parser
#     diagnostics. ifquery stderr, error/traceback output and unknown syntax
#     messages fail closed. The only rc=0 syntax warning accepted automatically
#     is "interface not recognized" for an interface that has its own stanza
#     describing a software-created interface. Required lower links are derived
#     from the complete parsed candidate, including non-auto VLAN dependencies.
#     Existing software interfaces are not subjected to physical .link pinning;
#     hardware-backed links must exist at runtime or be reproducible by staged
#     .link pinning matched to a detected NIC's persistent hardware MAC.
#   - The current live configuration is checked only as an advisory before the
#     restore session starts. A diagnostic can be overridden explicitly with
#     CONTINUE so a broken/missing live interfaces file does not prevent recovery
#     from a good backup. Isolation failures and an unresolved ifupdown2 lock
#     remain hard refusals. No pre-restore snapshot/retention run is triggered
#     merely by an advisory refusal.
#   - [SUPERSEDED later in this 1.8 draft] An earlier REVIEW3 replacement path
#     removed the destination before cp -a to avoid writes through destination
#     symlinks. The later sibling-staging/mv implementation below replaces that
#     mechanism. Snapshot existence still records files, directories and dangling
#     symlinks, and rollback equality checks file type/symlink target and content.
#   - The Proxmox network configuration lock (/etc/network/.pve-interfaces.lock)
#     is held from restore-session setup through validation/apply/rollback. The
#     candidate /etc/network tree is captured BEFORE validation; both ifquery and
#     the private ifreload syntax check read that captured tree, and the live tree
#     must still match it before apply or successful no-apply completion. Parser
#     sources outside /etc/network/interfaces.d and symlinks inside interfaces.d
#     are refused so the validated parser input cannot change behind the snapshot.
#   - ifupdown2 rc 89 is retried for a bounded 30-second window with increasing
#     delays and reported separately from validation and mount-namespace errors.
#     Live apply remains strict. After a failed live apply, rollback still
#     requires byte/type-identical old files plus a successful strict re-apply.
#   - If a target bridge is STP-off/no/default-off with a forward delay outside
#     the kernel STP range 2..30 while the existing runtime bridge is not unambiguously
#     stp_state=0, live apply is not offered. This avoids one-step ERANGE
#     transitions; the restored files are left for a controlled reboot instead.
#     At the 1.8 stage, Bridge-MTU remained a separate C-27 limitation; it is
#     addressed later in the 1.9 C-27 section.
#   - The post-write validation window also fingerprints ifupdown2's configured
#     ifstatenew file. state_dir is read with RawConfigParser-compatible semantics;
#     daemon mode is refused because ifupdown2d would run outside the validation
#     mount namespace. A foreign live apply that finishes between our lock probes
#     or while the user is at the apply/no-apply prompt is therefore treated like
#     concurrency: old files are restored and strictly re-applied instead of
#     claiming that runtime state was untouched.
#   - Network archive structure is preflighted from the protected backup before
#     the pre-restore snapshot. Symlinks/hardlinks/special objects in restored
#     interfaces.d or pinning trees are refused, and staged external source paths
#     are not accepted by C-26 validation.
#   - Network object replacement now copies to a private sibling first and uses
#     no-clobber live-path transitions plus postcondition checks. The source is
#     checked before changing the destination, mountpoints are refused, and
#     detected concurrent live objects are preserved before rollback instead of
#     being silently overwritten or discarded.
# 1.7 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, 2026-09-26)
#   - C-01: The backup service check uses ActiveState/SubState. A running
#     Type=oneshot service is "activating", which `systemctl is-active`
#     reports as not active, so the previous check never detected a running
#     backup. The timer flag is only set after the timer was really stopped.
#   - C-02: Before config.db is touched, pve-cluster is stopped
#     unconditionally under the runtime mask. "Stopped" now means ActiveState
#     inactive/failed, no /etc/pve mount and no running pmxcfs process.
#     Previously a unit in "activating", "deactivating" or auto-restart was
#     treated as stopped without a stop call. The mask itself is verified
#     (is-enabled must report masked-runtime).
#   - C-03: The start rate limit is reset (systemctl reset-failed) before an
#     intentional pve-cluster start. A replacement database that makes pmxcfs
#     exit uses up the limit through Restart=on-failure, and systemd then
#     also refused the start of the rollback database.
#   - C-04: Firewall reload/restart is invoked explicitly through systemd
#     (systemctl reload-or-restart pve-firewall), and pvesm status is run with
#     the restore/backup lock descriptors closed. On current PVE, the normal
#     `pve-firewall restart` CLI already delegates to systemd when invoked
#     outside PID 1; this change therefore makes that behavior explicit and
#     keeps descriptor handling defensive instead of fixing a direct-daemon
#     inheritance bug.
#   - C-05: Required backup members (sshd_config, interfaces, storage.cfg,
#     user.cfg, priv/shadow.cfg) are checked before the restore session
#     starts, as R-06 does for the firewall. A missing member is a normal
#     refusal instead of an "unexpected failure" with the timer left stopped.
#   - C-06: Write failures in pmxcfs restores (firewall, storage, users, VM)
#     lead into the rollback path instead of exiting with a partially applied
#     state. Rollback steps are checked individually, and only files that
#     were actually written are rolled back. restore_pmxcfs_from_stage is no
#     longer used and was removed.
#   - C-07: archive_has_prefix fails closed when the archive cannot be
#     listed. A listing error was read as "not present", and the live
#     sshd_config.d, interfaces.d or pinning directory was deleted without
#     replacement.
#   - C-08: sqlite3 runs with -batch -init /dev/null. A ~/.sqliterc of root
#     (for example ".headers on") changed the output, and every integrity
#     check failed.
#   - C-09: Menu numbers accept only 1 to 5 digits without a leading zero.
#     "08" terminated the tool in the VM selection, "010" was read as octal.
#   - C-10: Failures of begin_restore_session and cancelled confirmations
#     wait for Enter. The menu cleared those messages immediately before.
#   - C-11: Informational output after a completed restore (pve-firewall
#     status, pvesm status, pveum, qm config) can no longer turn a completed
#     restore into an "unexpected failure".
#   - C-12: VM restore refuses a live configuration with a "lock:" entry,
#     warns when the backup configuration contains one, and holds the Proxmox
#     per-VM lock (/var/lock/qemu-server/lock-<vmid>.conf) while writing and
#     validating. After the lock is acquired, VMID conflicts and the running
#     state are checked again so a qm start/migration that won the lock race
#     cannot finish first and leave a running/moved VM to be overwritten.
#   - C-13: Messages of the validation commands are shown and must be
#     accepted with KEEP, otherwise the restore is rolled back. The Proxmox
#     parsers usually only warn about invalid lines.
#   - C-14: When the original pmxcfs cannot be restarted, the tool reports
#     the pve-cluster state, a remaining runtime mask and the commands to
#     continue.
#   - C-15: Session start and end, critical states and unexpected exits are
#     written to the journal (logger -t pve-config-restore). An ERR trap
#     reports line and command of an unexpected failure.
#   - C-16: A failed verification from menu 1 or 10 returns to the menu;
#     menu 10 keeps the previous selection.
#   - C-17: Leftover protected copies (.restore-selected.*) are reported at
#     startup.
#   - C-18: The protected copy is restricted to mode 0700 after copying;
#     cp -a had applied the mode of the source directory.
#   - C-19: /usr/local/lib/systemd and /var/lock/qemu-server are created with
#     mode 0755 if missing, instead of 0700 from umask 077.
#   - C-20: The exit message no longer claims "No changes made".
#   - C-21: Formatting: restored line continuation in restore_vm_config and
#     comment order in restore_config_db.
#   - C-22: Version bump to 1.7 and this changelog.
#   - C-23: Commands newly used by the 1.7 safety helpers (install and sed)
#     are part of the startup prerequisite check instead of being assumed.
#   - C-24: While the KEEP question after a VM restore is open, the Proxmox
#     per-VM lock stays held (it has to, see C-12). The question now says so:
#     qm start, backups and other Proxmox operations on this VM fail with a
#     lock timeout (usually after 10 seconds) until it is answered.
#   - C-25: Review note on C-04: "outside PID 1" means that the parent
#     process of the pve-firewall CLI is not PID 1, i.e. the CLI was not
#     started by systemd (getppid() != 1 in PVE::Daemon). The first draft of
#     C-04 described a direct-daemon inheritance bug; that description was
#     wrong and was replaced in review round 2.
# 1.6 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, 2026-09-26)
#   - G-01: Backup config.db verification no longer depends on SQLite URI
#     filename support. The database is copied to a private temporary directory
#     and checked there with a normal sqlite3 open, so the selected backup remains
#     untouched even if SQLite creates WAL/SHM helper files.
#   - G-02: extract_tree and the VM-config archive listing capture tar pipeline
#     failures explicitly instead of losing them through Bash process
#     substitution.
#   - G-03: Emergency config.db recovery now refuses to replace the database if
#     SQLite journal/WAL/SHM sidecars still exist after the clean, runtime-masked
#     pve-cluster stop. This keeps the original database plus sidecars intact
#     instead of relying on a later sidecar reconstruction during rollback.
#   - G-04: Versionssprung auf 1.6 und dieses Changelog.
# 1.5 (DRAFT/ENTWURF, 2026-09-25)
#   - R-01: pin_selected_backup checks every step explicitly. It runs inside
#     `begin_restore_session || return 0`, where Bash ignores `set -e`. A
#     failing mktemp previously turned the copy into
#     `cp -a -- "${BACKUP}/." "/"` (files in / and / set to mode 0700).
#   - R-02: verify_backup_path fails explicitly on SHA-256 and tar errors
#     (previously ignored in the same context) and opens config.db explicitly
#     read-only with immutable=1 so verification no longer changes mtime.
#   - R-03: cleanup runs with `set +e`, so a failing message cannot abort
#     the remaining cleanup steps.
#   - R-04: HUP trap and signal-protected critical sections. An SSH
#     disconnect during an active restore previously restarted the backup
#     timer and deleted the rollback copies.
#   - R-05: Emergency config.db restore restarts the original pmxcfs if a
#     step fails before replacement. A failed sync after replacement or
#     rollback is critical and prevents automatic activation/reboot. Before a
#     rollback, pve-cluster must be verifiably stopped. If no config.db existed
#     before, pve-cluster stays stopped instead of starting with an empty
#     configuration. A missing rollback copy is reported as such. If SQLite
#     sidecars from an unclean shutdown were already removed when a later step
#     fails, the original database is not restarted automatically. While the
#     live database is offline, pve-cluster is runtime-masked so another
#     systemd activation cannot reopen pmxcfs during replacement/rollback; its
#     state is also re-checked before the live database is touched. Every
#     fail-closed path warns against reboot/start until manual verification.
#   - R-06: Firewall restore checks for optional host.fw/cluster.fw before
#     the restore session starts and no longer exits the tool mid-session.
#   - R-07: Files in /etc/pve are written via temporary file and rename.
#   - R-08: Emergency config.db restore is refused when either the local
#     corosync or the pmxcfs cluster configuration is present. The local file
#     is checked first, so pmxcfs is only accessed when it is absent.
#   - R-09: Timer messages state that an enabled timer restarts on reboot.
#   - R-10: Version bump to 1.5 and this changelog.
#   - R-11: The pre-restore backup run and `ifreload -a` do not inherit the
#     lock file descriptors (long-running helpers could keep the locks).
#   - R-12: extract_tree uses --no-recursion. Previously every directory
#     with at least one file (sshd_config.d, interfaces.d, pinning .link
#     files) made tar exit with status 2 ("Not found in archive").
# 1.4
#   - Baseline of this revision (no changelog before).
# ============================================================

SCRIPT_VERSION="1.14"
BASE="/var/lib/vz/host-config-backups"
